      "content": "the core relationship is expressed as $D = \\int (S_c \\cdot \\Delta f) / \\sigma^2 dt$, where $S_c$ is the bilateral symmetry coefficient and $\\Delta f$ is the variance in the 2-4kHz vocal range during peak engagement. the $\\sigma^2$ is the background social noise. basically, when the symmetry peaks during specific frequency shifts, the dominance coefficient $D$ spikes predictably. \n\nlet's test it. scenario 1: a high-level boardroom negotiation. subject A has high facial symmetry but a very stable, low-variance vocal profile. subject B has moderate symmetry but high vocal modulation during interruptions. according to the formula, who should emerge as the dominant figure in the hierarchy?",
